cemetery in recent times. A year earlier, on April 14, 1971, a staff member at the Ulstorff Cemetery in Hamburg entered the mortuary and stumbled across a horrific scene. The body of a girl had been removed from her coffin and posed so that she was leaning against it. She was naked and her lips and neck were bruised with visible bite marks. Placed beside her were two burnt-out candles. She was surrounded by the bodies of other corpses that had also been removed from their
公墓发生的一系列令人不安的事件之一。一年前，即1971年4月14日，汉堡乌尔斯多夫（Ulstorff）公墓的一名工作人员走进停尸房，无意中撞见了一个可怕的场景。一个女孩的尸体从棺材里被取了出来，并被摆成靠着棺材的姿势。她是赤裸的，她的嘴唇和脖子上有明显的咬痕淤青。在她身旁放着两根烧尽的蜡烛。她被其他同样从

